</style> <main class="w-content ">
      <div class="wrapper no-padding">
        
         <div class="container-system">

<div class="breadcrumb">
    <a class="active" href="https://firstsportz.com">Home</a>

            <a class="parentCrumbs" href="https://firstsportz.com/category/nba/">
            NBA        </a>
    </div>


<div class="layout-flex">
           <div class="single-post">
            <section class="section-intro">
               <div class="intro">
                  <h1>Which teams have never lost in the NBA Finals?</h1>
                                     <p>To remain undefeated at the biggest stage of the championship throughout franchise history has been a feat achieved by only a few NBA teams.</p>
                  <hr>
               </div>
               


               <div class="share-and-author">
    <div class="author">
        <span>By&nbsp;</span>
        <span>
            <a href="https://firstsportz.com/author/anjum-ashraf-rajonno/">
                <strong>Anjum Ash.</strong>
            </a>
        </span>
        <br>
                <span>Updated&nbsp;</span>
        <span><strong>Jan 20, 2024 / 10:33 EST</strong></span><br>
    </div>  

    <div align="right" class="share">
        <div onclick="window.location.href='https://news.google.com/publications/CAAqBwgKMM2KnQsw3pS1Aw?hl=en-IN&#038;gl=IN&#038;ceid=IN%3Aen'" class="shareIconGnews" style="z-index: 1; border: 1px solid #d1d1d1 !important; border-radius: 34px !important; width: fit-content !important; gap: 4px; text-decoration: none !important; font-weight: bold; display: flex !important; height: 35px !important; align-items: center !important; padding: 8px 12px 8px 10px !important;">
            <img style="width: 35px !important;" src="https://firstsportz.com/wp-content/themes/FS/assets/img/google-news.png" alt="Follow On Google News"> Follow Us
        </div>
    </div>
</div>


<div class="selfie-and-desc">
<div class="img">
                <div class="post-thumbnail">
            <img width="1200" height="900" src="https://firstsportz.com/wp-content/uploads/2023/03/Teams-that-have-never-lost-the-NBA-Finals.jpg" class="no-lazy" alt="Which teams have never lost in the NBA Finals?" loading="eager" fetchpriority="high" sizes="(max-width: 768px) 100vw, (min-width: 769px) 1600px" decoding="async" srcset="https://firstsportz.com/wp-content/uploads/2023/03/Teams-that-have-never-lost-the-NBA-Finals.jpg 1200w, https://firstsportz.com/wp-content/uploads/2023/03/Teams-that-have-never-lost-the-NBA-Finals-600x450.jpg 600w, https://firstsportz.com/wp-content/uploads/2023/03/Teams-that-have-never-lost-the-NBA-Finals-768x576.jpg 768w, https://firstsportz.com/wp-content/uploads/2023/03/Teams-that-have-never-lost-the-NBA-Finals-150x113.jpg 150w" />        </div>
    </div>



            <div class="img-info">
            <p>Teams that have never lost the NBA Finals (Image: FS)</p>
        </div>
    

    <div class="desc">
        
<p class="wp-block-paragraph">The NBA Finals have been the ultimate decider of the championship crown since the first NBA Finals in 1947. A total of 77 teams have lifted the title till date. Decided in a best of seven games format, the final series is the last showdown between Conference champions on their way to title Glory. But how many teams have not lost in the NBA Finals in the history of the league? </p>



<p class="wp-block-paragraph">To return with the title every time from an <a href="https://firstsportz.com/category/nba-latest-news-and-fixtures/" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer noopener">NBA</a> Final is no petty feat. To remain undefeated at the biggest stage of the championship throughout franchise history, has been achieved by very few NBA teams. </p><div class='code-block code-block-4' style='margin: 0 auto 26px auto; text-align: center; align-content: center; display: block; clear: both;  min-height: 250px; width: 100%;'>
<div style="display:flex;justify-content:center;align-items:center;height:100%;">
  <div id="dsk-box-ad-c"></div>
  <div id="mob-box-ad-a"></div>
</div>
</div>




<p class="wp-block-paragraph">Michael Jordan&#8217;s stellar record of <a href="https://firstsportz.com/nba-michael-jordan-rings/" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer noopener">six championships in six finals</a> is one of his many legendary accomplishments. But to have done so as Finals MVP is another incredible feat entirely. That, however, is Jordan&#8217;s record across his 15 seasons in the NBA. But in a franchise&#8217;s history, through the ups and downs, it is near impossible to maintain a 100% Finals-win record &#8211; and very, very few teams have managed to do so. So, who are the teams that have never lost in the NBA Finals?</p>



<p class="wp-block-paragraph"><div id="wpgtrRelated"><strong>Also Read</strong>: <a href="https://firstsportz.com/nba-which-teams-have-lost-the-most-nba-finals/" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer noopener">Which teams have lost the most NBA Finals?</a></div></p>



<h2 class="wp-block-heading" id="h-which-teams-have-never-lost-in-the-nba-finals">Which teams have never lost in the NBA Finals?</h2>



<p class="wp-block-paragraph">Only four teams have recorded a hundred percent win percentage in the NBA Finals to date. The list includes the <strong>Chicago Bulls, Toronto Raptors, Baltimore Bullets</strong> and <strong>Rochester Royals</strong>.</p><div class='code-block code-block-6' style='margin: 0 auto 26px auto; text-align: center; align-content: center; display: block; clear: both;  min-height: 250px; width: 100%;'>
<div style="display:flex;justify-content:center;align-items:center;height:100%;">
  <div style="display:none;" continuous-ad-container>
    <div class="dsk-box-ad-z"></div>
    <div class="mob-box-ad-z"></div>
  </div>
</div>
</div>




<figure class="wp-block-image size-large"><img decoding="async" width="1024" height="682" src="https://firstsportz.com/wp-content/uploads/2023/03/Picsart_23-03-28_10-07-36-242-1024x682.jpg" alt="Teams that never lost nba finals " class="wp-image-1097343" title="Which teams have never lost in the NBA Finals? 1" srcset="https://firstsportz.com/wp-content/uploads/2023/03/Picsart_23-03-28_10-07-36-242-1024x682.jpg 1024w, https://firstsportz.com/wp-content/uploads/2023/03/Picsart_23-03-28_10-07-36-242-300x200.jpg 300w, https://firstsportz.com/wp-content/uploads/2023/03/Picsart_23-03-28_10-07-36-242-768x512.jpg 768w, https://firstsportz.com/wp-content/uploads/2023/03/Picsart_23-03-28_10-07-36-242-1536x1024.jpg 1536w, https://firstsportz.com/wp-content/uploads/2023/03/Picsart_23-03-28_10-07-36-242-scaled.jpg 2048w, https://firstsportz.com/wp-content/uploads/2023/03/Picsart_23-03-28_10-07-36-242-150x100.jpg 150w, https://firstsportz.com/wp-content/uploads/2023/03/Picsart_23-03-28_10-07-36-242-750x500.jpg 750w, https://firstsportz.com/wp-content/uploads/2023/03/Picsart_23-03-28_10-07-36-242-1140x760.jpg 1140w" sizes="(max-width: 1024px) 100vw, 1024px" /><figcaption class="wp-element-caption">The Chicago Bulls have won 6 out of 6 NBA Finals (via AFP)</figcaption></figure>



<p class="wp-block-paragraph">Out of the four, only the <a href="https://firstsportz.com/category/nba-latest-news-and-fixtures/chicago-bulls/" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer noopener">Chicago Bulls</a> have appeared in more than one NBA Finals series and have never lost. In fact, they have played six NBA Finals series in their franchise history and haven&#8217;t lost a single one of them.</p>



<h2 class="wp-block-heading">Chicago Bulls</h2>



<p class="wp-block-paragraph">The Chicago Bulls have been in six NBA Finals in their franchise history and won all six titles. They did so in two three-peats in the same decade between 1991 to 1993, and then from 1996 to 1998.</p>



<p class="wp-block-paragraph">In their first ever Finals series, the Bulls beat the <a href="https://firstsportz.com/category/nba-latest-news-and-fixtures/los-angeles-lakers/" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer noopener">Los Angeles Lakers</a> 1-4 in just five games in 1991. The following season, they beat the Portland Trail Blazers 2-4 in six games to lift the title.</p>



<figure class="wp-block-image size-full"><img decoding="async" width="1024" height="768" src="https://firstsportz.com/wp-content/uploads/2024/01/Michael-Jordan-NBA-Championship.jpg" alt="Michael Jordan NBA Championship" class="wp-image-1686262" title="Which teams have never lost in the NBA Finals? 2" srcset="https://firstsportz.com/wp-content/uploads/2024/01/Michael-Jordan-NBA-Championship.jpg 1024w, https://firstsportz.com/wp-content/uploads/2024/01/Michael-Jordan-NBA-Championship-600x450.jpg 600w, https://firstsportz.com/wp-content/uploads/2024/01/Michael-Jordan-NBA-Championship-768x576.jpg 768w, https://firstsportz.com/wp-content/uploads/2024/01/Michael-Jordan-NBA-Championship-150x113.jpg 150w" sizes="(max-width: 1024px) 100vw, 1024px" /></figure>



<p class="wp-block-paragraph">In the 1993 Finals, Chicago Bulls defeated the <a href="https://firstsportz.com/category/nba-latest-news-and-fixtures/phoenix-suns/" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer noopener">Phoenix Suns</a> 2-4 in the six-game series, completing their iconic three-peat. So far, having won all three Finals series in franchise history, the Bulls made their next Finals appearance in 1996.</p><div class='code-block code-block-6' style='margin: 0 auto 26px auto; text-align: center; align-content: center; display: block; clear: both;  min-height: 250px; width: 100%;'>
<div style="display:flex;justify-content:center;align-items:center;height:100%;">
  <div style="display:none;" continuous-ad-container>
    <div class="dsk-box-ad-z"></div>
    <div class="mob-box-ad-z"></div>
  </div>
</div>
</div>




<p class="wp-block-paragraph">They faced the Seattle SuperSonics in their fourth Finals in franchise history, winning the Championship 2-4 in six games. In the following two seasons, the Bulls beat the Utah Jazz twice in two NBA Finals, lifting their fifth and sixth Championship title.</p>



<h2 class="wp-block-heading" id="h-toronto-raptors">Toronto Raptors</h2>



<p class="wp-block-paragraph">The <a href="https://firstsportz.com/category/nba-latest-news-and-fixtures/toronto-raptors/" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer noopener">Toronto Raptors</a> made their first ever NBA Finals in 2018-2019 against the Golden State Warriors. The Dubs were the defending Champions at the time and had won the last two Championships on the trot, eyeing a three-peat.</p>



<figure class="wp-block-image size-full"><img decoding="async" width="1200" height="900" src="https://firstsportz.com/wp-content/uploads/2024/01/Raptors-celebrate-NBA-Championship.webp" alt="Raptors celebrate NBA Championship" class="wp-image-1686291" title="Which teams have never lost in the NBA Finals? 3" srcset="https://firstsportz.com/wp-content/uploads/2024/01/Raptors-celebrate-NBA-Championship.webp 1200w, https://firstsportz.com/wp-content/uploads/2024/01/Raptors-celebrate-NBA-Championship-600x450.webp 600w, https://firstsportz.com/wp-content/uploads/2024/01/Raptors-celebrate-NBA-Championship-768x576.webp 768w, https://firstsportz.com/wp-content/uploads/2024/01/Raptors-celebrate-NBA-Championship-150x113.webp 150w" sizes="(max-width: 1200px) 100vw, 1200px" /><figcaption class="wp-element-caption">Raptors celebrate their NBA Championship (via Imago)</figcaption></figure>



<p class="wp-block-paragraph">Going as the underdogs, the Raptors beat the Warriors 2-4 in six games, lifting their first ever championship in their first-ever NBA Finals. Their victory denied the Dubs dynasty a three-peat of titles, for the second time in the same decade.</p>



<h2 class="wp-block-heading">Rochester Royals</h2>



<p class="wp-block-paragraph">The Rochester Royals made their only NBA Finals way back in the 1950-51 season. They beat the New York Knicks 4-3 in seven games.</p><div class='code-block code-block-6' style='margin: 0 auto 26px auto; text-align: center; align-content: center; display: block; clear: both;  min-height: 250px; width: 100%;'>
<div style="display:flex;justify-content:center;align-items:center;height:100%;">
  <div style="display:none;" continuous-ad-container>
    <div class="dsk-box-ad-z"></div>
    <div class="mob-box-ad-z"></div>
  </div>
</div>
</div>




<figure class="wp-block-image size-full"><img decoding="async" width="1200" height="900" src="https://firstsportz.com/wp-content/uploads/2024/01/Rochester-Royals-Championship-winning-team.webp" alt="The Championship winning Rochester Royals team" class="wp-image-1686305" title="Which teams have never lost in the NBA Finals? 4" srcset="https://firstsportz.com/wp-content/uploads/2024/01/Rochester-Royals-Championship-winning-team.webp 1200w, https://firstsportz.com/wp-content/uploads/2024/01/Rochester-Royals-Championship-winning-team-600x450.webp 600w, https://firstsportz.com/wp-content/uploads/2024/01/Rochester-Royals-Championship-winning-team-768x576.webp 768w, https://firstsportz.com/wp-content/uploads/2024/01/Rochester-Royals-Championship-winning-team-150x113.webp 150w" sizes="(max-width: 1200px) 100vw, 1200px" /><figcaption class="wp-element-caption">The Championship winning Rochester Royals team (via BFrames vault)</figcaption></figure>



<p class="wp-block-paragraph">It was their only NBA title in franchise history. They never made another Finals.</p>



<h2 class="wp-block-heading">Baltimore Bullets</h2>



<p class="wp-block-paragraph">Back in the 1947-48 NBA Finals, it was the Baltimore Bullets who made it to one of the first finals hosted by the league.</p>



<figure class="wp-block-image size-full is-resized"><img decoding="async" width="1200" height="900" src="https://firstsportz.com/wp-content/uploads/2024/01/Baltimore-Bullest-Championship-winning-team.webp" alt="The Championship winning Baltimore Bullets team" class="wp-image-1686306" style="aspect-ratio:1.3333333333333333;width:816px;height:auto" title="Which teams have never lost in the NBA Finals? 5" srcset="https://firstsportz.com/wp-content/uploads/2024/01/Baltimore-Bullest-Championship-winning-team.webp 1200w, https://firstsportz.com/wp-content/uploads/2024/01/Baltimore-Bullest-Championship-winning-team-600x450.webp 600w, https://firstsportz.com/wp-content/uploads/2024/01/Baltimore-Bullest-Championship-winning-team-768x576.webp 768w, https://firstsportz.com/wp-content/uploads/2024/01/Baltimore-Bullest-Championship-winning-team-150x113.webp 150w" sizes="(max-width: 1200px) 100vw, 1200px" /><figcaption class="wp-element-caption">The Championship winning Baltimore Bullets team (via FromTheBend archives)</figcaption></figure>



<p class="wp-block-paragraph">They faced the Philadelphia Warriors in a six-game series, winning 4-2 to lift one of the first NBA titles in league history. But needless to say, no other franchise has been successful in replicating the dominance of Michael Jordan&#8217;s Chicago Bulls when it comes to Finals win percentage.</p>



<h4 class="wp-block-heading" id="h-faqs">FAQs</h4>



<div class="schema-faq wp-block-yoast-faq-block"><div class="schema-faq-section" id="faq-question-1705745666594"><strong class="schema-faq-question">Q. How many Finals have the Chicago Bulls played?</strong> <p class="schema-faq-answer">The Chicago Bulls played six NBA Finals.</p><div class='code-block code-block-6' style='margin: 0 auto 26px auto; text-align: center; align-content: center; display: block; clear: both;  min-height: 250px; width: 100%;'>
